# Fair value-policy comparison

Same engineering base (same gate, tools, prompt, model, turn and time budget); only GUI_GATE_VALUE_POLICY differs.
Seeds are independent repeats (no sampling seed reaches the model API).

| policy | planned runs | success | rate | Wilson 95% | valid runs | valid rate | infra/missing | mean wall_s |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| vp_direct | 60 | 60 | 1.000 | 0.940-1.000 | 60 | 1.000 | 0 | 100.0 |
| vp_learned | 60 | 59 | 0.983 | 0.911-0.997 | 59 | 1.000 | 1 | 60.0 |

## Paired (task level)

| policy | vs | tasks | diff | 95% CI | permutation p | McNemar n01/n10 | McNemar p |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| vp_learned | vp_direct | 20 | -0.017 | -0.050..+0.000 | 1.0000 | 0/1 | 1.0000 |

## Non-inferiority (paired, one-sided, task level)

| policy | vs | margin | diff | one-sided lower | p | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| vp_learned | vp_direct | 0.100 | -0.017 | -0.050 | 0.0002 | non-inferior |

- vp_learned: non-inferior within the pre-registered margin: the success rate difference is -0.017, one-sided 95% lower bound -0.050 > -0.100 (p = 0.0002).

## Budget curve (success within wall_s budget, planned runs)

| budget | vp_direct | vp_learned |
|---|---|---|
| 60 | 0.000 | 0.983 |
| 100 | 1.000 | 0.983 |

A non-significant difference is not evidence of equality; claims need a pre-registered margin.

